WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
David Packman Show at David Packman Dot.com.

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:05.259
We were scheduled to have four more Democratic
primary elections yesterday.

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:06.259
One was canceled.

00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:11.760
That's Ohio, thanks to Republican Governor
Mike DeWine deciding that because of Corona

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.790
virus, Ohio would be postponing its primary.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.900
In the end, it didn't matter.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.520
The three that we had went to Joe Biden and
Bernie Sanders has announced he will be reassessing

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:26.220
his campaign, which is political code for
it's over.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.220
Let's look at the numbers.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.220
Let's look at what took place.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:34.179
Three elections happened last night, Arizona,
Florida and Illinois going into yesterday

00:00:34.179 --> 00:00:35.370
in terms of delegates.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:42.510
Joe Biden was leading Bernie Sanders by 151
delegates, 894 to 7:43.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:46.960
The results in yesterday's three primaries
are and of course, we like to compare to the

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.999
polling in Arizona.

00:00:48.999 --> 00:00:55.579
Biden was winning by 18 in the polls, but
won only by 12 in Florida.

00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:58.920
Biden was winning by thirty nine and won by
thirty nine.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.969
And in Illinois, Biden was winning by twenty
nine and one by twenty three.

00:01:03.969 --> 00:01:09.000
Biden underperforming the polls in two of
yesterday's three primaries.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:16.190
This now pushes the delegate numbers to eleven
forty seven for Biden, 861 for Bernie.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:17.190
Doing the math for you.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.189
That's a 286 delegate lead for Joe Biden.

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:26.750
Now, as I had said before, if the delegate
lead ends at more than 200 after the March

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:31.859
17 primaries and certainly if it ends at more
than 250.

00:01:31.859 --> 00:01:36.510
Bernie should suspend his campaign simply
because he has no path to the nomination.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:40.979
And indeed, Bernie Sanders has announced he
is now assessing his campaign.

00:01:40.979 --> 00:01:46.530
He says in the following weeks now, this again
is how you translate telegraph in political

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:48.140
code that it's over.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:53.619
It's just a matter of when and how they structure
his exit in order to be as graceful as possible.

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:56.760
And to be clear, this really isn't close.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.969
It's not you know, maybe if he sticks it out.

00:01:58.969 --> 00:02:00.039
It is not close.

00:02:00.039 --> 00:02:03.670
It's not clear Bernie has a path to winning
any more.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:06.070
States may be won here or there.

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:08.670
The popular vote count is not close.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:14.720
It is now about 2.5 million votes, a 4 in
favor of Joe Biden.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:18.800
I said yesterday, you know, it may end up
larger than 2 million.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.880
And I underestimated by about 25 percent.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.790
Joe Biden leading by 2.5 million votes.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:25.930
It's a massive lead.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:28.550
And this is not about, you know, doing more
post-mortems.

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:29.550
We've done post-mortems.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.770
We're in the middle of a crisis with the virus.

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:34.550
This is simply about it's not at all close.

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:38.380
And again, when Bernie will suspend, we don't
know.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:43.390
We know that there was scheduled to be a March
24 primary in Georgia, which Biden was going

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:44.490
to win easily.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:46.470
That's been postponed because of the virus.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:50.620
Puerto Rico scheduled to vote on March 29
in April.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:54.630
On April 4th, Alaska and Hawaii were scheduled
as well as Wyoming.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:57.720
Again, not not very many delegates there.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.190
April 7th in Wisconsin.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:03.660
Twenty eighth of April, we were getting to
Connecticut, Delaware, Maryland, New York,

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.290
Pennsylvania and Rhode Island.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:09.910
We have no idea whether those were going to
be postponed or will be.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.830
But every indication I mean, listen, it's
we just don't know.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:13.830
It's possible.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.850
By the time you listen to this, Bernie will
be out.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:16.850
It's possible.

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:21.690
Bernie really will take a couple of weeks,
given that we don't have any primaries coming

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:22.780
up in the immediate.

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:26.670
Other than Puerto Rico scheduled eleven days
from now, I don't know.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.670
It's not clear what it makes sense to do.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:33.700
And of course, we will be forced into discussing,
are we going to have conventions?

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:34.700
Are we going?

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:40.110
You know, how will the virus affect the remaining
trajectory of the primary?

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.740
The primary in all.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:49.080
But the most technical sense is over as Joe
Biden has won three more primaries and easily.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:52.290
And the big news, Bernie Sanders assessing
his campaign.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:56.900
We deal with things as they are, not as as
not as we would wish them to be.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.540
And these are the numbers we are dealing with.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:04.570
I still had people tweet angrily tweeting
me today when I was commenting on Bernie's

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:09.180
announcement that he is assessing, which is
code for ending soon, saying, I am redoubling

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.600
down my efforts and donating money to Bernie.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:15.750
I mean, I don't get you know, you whatever
your financial situation is, if you want to

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.970
donate to Bernie now, do it.

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:21.400
But to some degree, it seems like denialism
at this point in time.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.691
And I don't totally get it.

00:04:22.691 --> 00:04:24.900
That's money that could be used.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.380
You know, it donate to some issue campaign.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:30.580
If you don't care about Biden beating, beating
Trump.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:31.580
Fine.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:32.940
But I don't know why.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:36.970
When Bernie says he's reassessing the campaign,
you would you would continue donating.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:38.570
But maybe somebody can let me know.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.630
This is the path forward.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:05:42.630
We will have more coverage

